# Allow-list. This is the other half of the bundling decision in
# scripts/build.mjs: everything except `vscode` is bundled into
# dist/extension.js, so node_modules must NOT ship. If build.mjs ever gains an
# `external` entry other than vscode, this file has to grow a matching
# !node_modules/... line or the extension will fail at first connect with
# "Cannot find module". The two files change together, always.
**
!dist/extension.js
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
# Only what the extension itself draws. The rest of resources/icons -- the
# light plate, the 128px copy, the plain marks -- exists for the readme and is
# served from the repository, so shipping it would be dead weight in every
# install.
!resources/dark/**
!resources/light/**
!resources/icons/syncx-icon-512.png
!resources/icons/syncx-activitybar.svg
!schema/**
